From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 08:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sysbus: drop the python2.7 test client role

The role is for a python2.7 test client:

  "exeName":"@WEBOS_INSTALL_BINDIR@/python2.7"

Python 2 has not been in the image for years, so the role can never match a
running process. ls-hubd loads it on every boot and do_validate_ls2_wiring
reports it as a role keyed on an executable that is not installed.

The python bindings under test/python are not packaged either; nothing
references this file from a build rule.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 files/sysbus/com.webos.media.client.python.role.json.in | 12 ---
 1 file changed, 12 deletion(s)

--- a/files/sysbus/com.webos.media.client.python.role.json.in
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,12 +0,0 @@
-{
-    "exeName":"@WEBOS_INSTALL_BINDIR@/python2.7",
-    "type": "regular",
-    "trustLevel" : "oem",
-    "allowedNames": ["com.webos.media.client.*"],
-    "permissions": [
-        {
-            "service":"com.webos.media.client.*",
-            "outbound":["com.webos.media"]
-        }
-    ]
-}
